<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Flow xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <apiVersion>58.0</apiVersion>
    <areMetricsLoggedToDataCloud>false</areMetricsLoggedToDataCloud>
    <decisions>
        <description>1. New case creation scenario - update the Manger fields if owner is a user and the manager is not null
2. Case update scenario - Owner changed and the new owner is a user not a queue  - OR the owner is not changed but manager is changed from user record (at least this update for an edit on case)
3. If the owner is a queue - create or update scenario</description>
        <name>Global_Service_case_update</name>
        <label>Global Service case update</label>
        <locationX>710</locationX>
        <locationY>287</locationY>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Default Outcome</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>For_new_case</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>CheckNewCase</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>true</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.OwnerId</leftValueReference>
                <operator>StartsWith</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <stringValue>005</stringValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.Owner:User.ManagerId</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Update_Owner_s_Manager_and_Owner_s_Manager_Manager</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>1- For new case</label>
        </rules>
        <rules>
            <name>For_Existing_case</name>
            <conditionLogic>(1 AND 2) OR (1 AND  3)</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.OwnerId</leftValueReference>
                <operator>StartsWith</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <stringValue>005</stringValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.OwnerId</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsChanged</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>true</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.IME_SC_Owner_Manager__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>NotEqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <elementReference>$Record.Owner:User.ManagerId</elementReference>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Owner_Manager_Check</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>2- For Existing case</label>
        </rules>
        <rules>
            <name>For_case_who_s_owner_is_Queue</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.OwnerId</leftValueReference>
                <operator>StartsWith</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <stringValue>00G</stringValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.IME_SC_Owner_Manager__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Update_Managers_name_as_blank</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>3- For case who&apos;s owner is Queue</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <decisions>
        <description>Checking if Owner Manager is blank or not</description>
        <name>Owner_Manager_Check</name>
        <label>Owner Manager Check</label>
        <locationX>578</locationX>
        <locationY>395</locationY>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Default Outcome</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Check_if_Owner_Manager_is_not_blank</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.Owner:User.ManagerId</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Update_Manager_and_OwnerManager_s_Manager</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>1-Check if Owner Manager is not blank</label>
        </rules>
        <rules>
            <name>Check_if_Owners_manager_is_blank</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.Owner:User.ManagerId</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>true</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Update_Managers_fields_as_blank</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>2- Check if Owners manager is blank</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <description>This flow updates the fields IME_SC_Owner_Manager__c and IME_SC_Manager_of_Manager_OwnerId__c to the case owner&apos;s manager and case owner managers&apos; manager respectively  #16378 - Keeping this on after flow as case assignment rule will not be considered in before flow and we are working on case owner.
#27471 : Included this functionality for NCSP record types, CLAS record types and Global Orders cases
#28035: Updated flow to before flow as after flow some scenarios were failing.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <description>To check if case is newly created</description>
        <name>CheckNewCase</name>
        <dataType>Boolean</dataType>
        <expression>ISNEW()</expression>
